  "aiInstructions": "You are writing the note a delivery lead reads before a solution call.\n\nWrite 200 to 280 words, second person, direct and technically literate. Name the ONE thing that would turn this project into a rewrite halfway through, using the dimension names as evidence. Say what it costs to start without it.\n\nDo NOT quote a price, do NOT estimate hours, team size or a delivery date, and do NOT propose an architecture or a stack. Describe the gap, then stop. The solution belongs on the call.\n\nNever promise a delivery timeline, never mention scores as numbers.",
